00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.890
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Give me a minute,

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.010
and I'll show you how Anthos
can help you rapidly build

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.100
and deploy hybrid and
multi-cloud applications

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.020
without compromising security
or increasing complexity.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.640
Anthos is a hybrid and
multi-cloud application

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.410
modernization platform.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.180
Embracing open
standards, it lets

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.870
you run your apps unmodified
on existing on-prem hardware

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:32.009
or in public cloud, simply,
flexibly, and securely.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:33.150
Can't wait to try it?

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.605
Set up your own
sample deployment

00:00:34.605 --> 00:00:37.800
at goo.gle/tryAnthos.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.200
Anthos enables
containerized microservices

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.950
architectural-based apps across
multiple platforms, clusters,

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.270
and locations.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.830
It allows for consistent policy
and configuration management,

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.570
provides observability
through golden signals,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.050
and delivers a Zero Trust
security model for your apps.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.460
Anthos can be used to
re-platform virtual machines,

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.320
modernize existing
apps, applying

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.349
modern CI/CD principles,
and security,

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:08.280
reduce operational expenditure
with no vendor lock-in

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.800
So next time you're
thinking about hybrid

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.930
and multi-cloud
application platforms,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.000
take a minute to look at Anthos.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.090
For more info, check out
cloud.google.com/anthos.

